{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Trade & Migration Office - Aerie Exchange{% endblock %}

{% block meta %}
	<meta name="description" content="The District's Trade & Migration Office: the tariff on imports, the migration regime and the tax on homes bought from outside the District.">
	<meta property="og:title" content="Trade & Migration Office | Aerie Exchange">
	<meta property="og:type" content="website">
{% endblock %}

{% macro law_line(law) %}
	<dl class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-x-6 gap-y-1 mt-4 text-xs">
		<div>
			<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">In force</dt>
			<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5 font-mono tabular-nums">{{ law.inForce|pct(2) }}</dd>
		</div>
		<div>
			<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Next budget</dt>
			<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5 font-mono tabular-nums">{{ law.next is null ? '–' : law.next|pct(2) }}</dd>
		</div>
		<div>
			<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">After the vote</dt>
			<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5 font-mono tabular-nums">{{ law.expected is null ? '–' : law.expected|pct(2) }}</dd>
		</div>
	</dl>
{% endmacro %}

{% block body %}
<div class="max-w-400 mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8 pb-12 w-full space-y-6">

	{% include 'government/_breadcrumb.html.twig' with {current: 'Trade & Migration Office'} %}
	<header class="pb-5 border-b border-outline-variant/15">
		<h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-on-surface tracking-tight">Trade &amp; Migration Office</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
			The office that collects the District's tariff, issues its work and residence permits and levies the tax on homes
			bought from outside the District. It sets none of them: each is a law the Diet passes in its budget, and the office
			carries out what the budget says.{% if office.expectedFrom %} Traders expect the laws the next government passes
			to take effect from {{ office.expectedFrom }}.{% endif %}
		</p>
	</header>

	{% set tariff = office.tariff %}
	<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="tariff-heading">
		<h2 id="tariff-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">The tariff on imports</h2>
		{{ _self.law_line(tariff) }}
		<p class="text-xs text-on-surface mt-4 max-w-3xl">
			{% if tariff.inForce > 0 %}
				Goods worth <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ tariff.goodsImportsToGdp|pct(0) }}</span> of GDP come in each year, and the tariff raises
				<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ tariff.revenueToGdp|pct(2) }}</span> of GDP from them. The District's partners answer with
				<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ tariff.retaliation|pct(1) }}</span> on its exports, and sheltered firms cost the economy
				<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ tariff.outputCost|pct(2) }}</span> of its output for as long as the tariff stands.
			{% else %}
				The District is a free port: goods worth <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ tariff.goodsImportsToGdp|pct(0) }}</span> of GDP come in each year without duty, and its exports meet none in return.
			{% endif %}
		</p>
	</section>

	<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
		{% set migration = office.migration %}
		<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="migration-heading">
			<h2 id="migration-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">Migration</h2>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Labour force growth a year, the newcomers the permits admit in it</p>
			{{ _self.law_line(migration) }}
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface mt-4 max-w-3xl">
				The District's own people add <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.natural|pct(2) }}</span> to its labour force a year, whatever the permits say.
				It opened admitting newcomers worth <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.structuralMigration|pct(2) }}</span> of the population a year on top, for a labour force growing <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.structural|pct(2) }}</span>.
				The permits have added <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.populationShift|pct(1, true) }}</span> to the population since, against that path.
				More come while jobs are plentiful and fewer while they are scarce: under these permits each point of unemployment below its usual level draws <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.jobsResponse|pct(2) }}</span> more a year{% if migration.cyclical|abs > 0.00005 %}, and the labour market is {{ migration.cyclical > 0 ? 'adding' : 'taking' }} <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.cyclical|abs|pct(2) }}</span> a year {{ migration.cyclical > 0 ? 'to' : 'from' }} the newcomers now{% endif %}.
			</p>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-3 leading-relaxed">
				The tightest regime the Diet can pass admits <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.closed|pct(2) }}</span> of the population a year, the most open
				<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ migration.open|pct(2) }}</span>. Newcomers need homes before they need jobs, so a rise in migration reaches house prices first. The more open the regime, the more migration answers the labour market.
			</p>
		</section>

		{% set buyers = office.foreignBuyers %}
		<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="buyers-heading">
			<h2 id="buyers-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">Homes bought from outside the District</h2>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Tax on the price, paid by a buyer who lives outside the District</p>
			{{ _self.law_line(buyers) }}
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface mt-4 max-w-3xl">
				{% if buyers.inForce > 0 %}
					It holds home prices <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ buyers.priceEffect|pct(1) }}</span> below where they would stand without it, as most buyers from outside stay away,
					and raises <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ buyers.revenueToGdp|pct(3) }}</span> of GDP a year from the few who still buy.
				{% else %}
					Homes are open to buyers from anywhere, as at Year 1.
				{% endif %}
				The highest rate the Diet can pass is <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ buyers.strictest|pct(0) }}</span>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<p class="source-note">{{ source_line('trade-migration-office') }}</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
